Commentary of al-Shinqiti (Adwa' al-Bayan) on surah 55, verse 2:

His saying, exalted is He: ﴿He taught the Qur'an﴾. That is, He taught His Prophet ﷺ the Qur'an, and his community received it from him. This noble verse contains God's rebuttal of the disbelievers in their claim that he (the Prophet) learned this Qur'an from a human being, as was mentioned earlier in His saying: ﴿And We certainly know that they say, "It is only a human who teaches him."﴾ [an-Nahl: 103], and His saying, exalted is He: ﴿So he reflected and calculated. Woe to him, how he calculated! Then he considered. Then he frowned and scowled. Then he turned away and was arrogant. And he said, "This is nothing but magic transmitted from others"﴾ [al-Muddaththir: 18–24], meaning: Muhammad relates it from someone else.

And His saying, exalted is He: ﴿And those who disbelieve say, "This is not but a falsehood he has invented, and other people have helped him at it." So they have certainly committed an injustice and a falsehood. And they say, "Tales of the former peoples which he has had written down, and they are dictated to him morning and afternoon."﴾ [al-Furqan: 4–5].

So His saying here, ﴿The Most Merciful﴾ ﴿taught the Qur'an﴾, means: the matter is not as you have mentioned, that he learned the Qur'an from a human being; rather, the Most Merciful, exalted is He and high is He, is the One who taught it to him. The verses indicating this are very numerous, such as:

• His saying, exalted is He: ﴿Say, "It was sent down by He who knows the secret within the heavens and the earth."﴾ [al-Furqan: 6];

• His saying, exalted is He: ﴿Alif, Lam, Ra. [This is] a Book whose verses have been perfected and then presented in detail from the Wise, the All-Aware﴾ [Hud: 1];

• His saying, exalted is He: ﴿Ha, Mim. A revelation from the Most Merciful, the Especially Merciful. A Book whose verses have been detailed as an Arabic Qur'an for a people who know, bringing good tidings and warning﴾ [Fussilat: 1–4];

• His saying, exalted is He: ﴿And We had certainly brought them a Book which We detailed with knowledge, as guidance and mercy for a people who believe﴾ [al-A'raf: 52];

• His saying, exalted is He: ﴿And thus We have sent it down as an Arabic Qur'an and have diversified therein from warning that perhaps they will fear Allah or it will cause them to remember﴾ [Ta-Ha: 113];

• His saying, exalted is He: ﴿And they do not come to you with an example except that We bring you the truth and better explanation﴾ [al-Furqan: 33];

• His saying, exalted is He: ﴿Indeed, upon Us is its collection and its recitation. So when We have recited it, then follow its recitation. Then upon Us is its clarification﴾ [al-Qiyamah: 17–19];

• His saying, exalted is He: ﴿And thus We have revealed to you an inspiration of Our command. You did not know what the Book was, nor [what] faith [was], but We have made it a light by which We guide whom We will of Our servants﴾ [ash-Shura: 52];

• His saying, exalted is He: ﴿We relate to you the best of stories in what We have revealed to you of this Qur'an, although you were before it among the unaware﴾ [Yusuf: 3];

• His saying, exalted is He: ﴿And He taught you what you did not know, and the bounty of Allah upon you has been great﴾ [an-Nisa': 113]. Among the greatest of that is this mighty Qur'an. And His saying: ﴿The month of Ramadan [is that] in which was revealed the Qur'an, a guidance for the people and clear proofs of guidance and criterion﴾ [al-Baqarah: 185].

His teaching this great Qur'an, exalted is He, has been explained in other places to be among the greatest of His blessings, as He said: ﴿Then We caused to inherit the Book those whom We have chosen of Our servants﴾ up to His saying: ﴿That is the great bounty﴾ [Fatir: 32].

Allah has also taught people to praise Him for this supreme blessing, which is the sending down of the Qur'an, in His saying: ﴿Praise be to Allah, who has sent down to His servant the Book and has not made therein any deviance﴾ [al-Kahf: 1]. He has also explained that its sending down is a mercy from Him to His creation, exalted is He, in verses of His Book, such as His saying: ﴿And you did not expect that the Book would be bestowed upon you, except as a mercy from your Lord﴾ [al-Qasas: 86], and His saying: ﴿Indeed, We were sending [a warning]. As a mercy from your Lord﴾ [ad-Dukhan: 5–6]. We have explained the verses clarifying this in (the surahs of) al-Kahf and az-Zukhruf.

﴿عَلَّمَ القُرْآنَ﴾ ("He taught the Qur'an"): one of the two objects has been omitted in it. The verified view is that the omitted one is the first object, not the second, as al-Fakhr ar-Razi thought; Abu Hayyan refuted him on this. The correct view is what he (al-Shinqiti) mentioned, that the omitted object is the first, and its estimated form is: "He taught the Prophet ﷺ," and it was said: "Jibril," and it was said: "man."
